          "editorMode": "code",
          "format": "table",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "-- What the car is running now: the open-ended setups that have already started.\nSELECT\n  COALESCE(\n    string_agg(initcap(replace(aspect, '_', ' ')) || ': ' || label, ' · ' ORDER BY aspect),\n    'No setup recorded'\n  ) AS \"current_setup\"\nFROM car_setups\nWHERE car_id IN ($car_id)\n  AND ended_at IS NULL\n  AND started_at <= current_date;\n",
          "refId": "A",
          "sql": {
            "columns": [
              {
                "parameters": [],
                "type": "function"
              }
            ],
            "groupBy": [
              {
                "property": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "type": "groupBy"
              }
            ],
            "limit": 50
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": "Current setup",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 18,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 3,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "### How drives are attributed\n\nA setup is **one aspect** of the car over an **inclusive** date range: the tyres\nthat were fitted, a trailer being towed, a roof box, a load. Aspects are\nindependent, so their ranges may overlap - fitting new tyres does not end a\nroof box period.\n\nEach drive is attributed to the **newest** setup of each aspect (the highest\nstart date) whose range covers the drive's **local calendar day**. That is the\nday the owner changed the setup, not the UTC day, so one drive can appear under\ntyres *and* under towing. Nothing is written onto the drive: correcting a date\nrange re-tags the history instead of leaving stale tags behind.\n\n**Not recorded** is the baseline for an aspect that has setups but none covering\na drive; it is what a tyre change, a trailer or a roof box is compared against.\nOnly aspects with at least one setup appear here - add one on the `/setups`\npage in the app.\n\nEnergy is the same estimate as the Efficiency dashboard: the preferred range\ndrop times the car's efficiency. Drives without a usable range drop are left\nout. The *min. distance per drive* filter excludes short trips, and the dashboard's time range limits the drives considered. The /setups page in the app applies neither, so its totals cover every drive.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.2.1",
      "title": "How setups are attributed",
      "type": "text"
    },
